# ~/.config/packages/Snapfile — snap packages for the Linux dev-shell.
#
# Format: one snap per line, "<name> [snap flags]". '#' starts a comment.
# `run_onchange_after_40-install-snaps` re-runs when this file changes and
# delegates to `system-package snap sync`, the same worker used by
# `system-update`. That worker installs missing declared snaps and refreshes
# declared snaps without trying to remove snapd-managed base/platform snaps.
#
# Reserve this for classic-confined apps that are better as snaps than as
# mise binaries. Do NOT list mise or atuin here:
#   - snap mise symlinks its tool shims to /snap/bin/mise, which breaks
#     shim execution (tools resolve to the snap dispatcher).
#   - snap atuin is strict-confined and cannot write ~/.local/share/atuin.
# Both of those come from mise / standalone installers instead.

nvim --classic
zellij --classic
